{
  "status": "Status: frozen (ADR-0119). Assigned values are immutable; a 'reserved...' construction may be filled once.",
  "registry": "om-object-types",
  "registry_version": 1,
  "rules": [
    "object_type ids are assigned here and never reused. 0 is reserved. 1..32767 = public registry; 32768..65279 = reserved for future public allocation; 65280..65535 = experimental/private (never valid in a production profile).",
    "A 'signed' type travels as a SignedEnvelope {1: body bstr, 2: [+ Signature]} whose body is the canonical encoding of the top-level object. Each signature is over DS-SIG(label, crypto_profile, role, signer, body) as defined in om-domain-separation.json.",
    "A 'hash' label defines the object's identity/chain hash: Digest = H(DS-HASH(label, body)). The hash covers the body only, never the signatures.",
    "max_bytes bounds the encoded top-level item (envelope included) and is checked before decoding."
  ],
